RCE_KEY': 'investing_comcryptonews', 'NAME': 'Investing.com Crypto News', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/106/default.png', 'URL': 'https://www.investing.com/rss/news_301.rss', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': 1505088000, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758044748, 'CREATED_ON': 1754907212, 'UPDATED_ON': 1754907484}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 51832832, 'GUID': 'https://cryptonews.com/?p=424179', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758044571, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/52/51832832.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Investors Brace for Fed Pivot as BTC & ETH Outflows Contrast Stablecoin Surge: CryptoQuant', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Tanzeel Akhtar', 'URL': 'https://cryptonews.com/news/investors-brace-for-fed-pivot-as-btc-eth-outflows-contrast-stablecoin-surge-cryptoquant/', 'SOURCE_ID': 52, 'BODY': 'Crypto markets are closely watching the U.S. Federal Reserve as speculation grows over a potential interest rate cut, reports CryptoQuant. Markets await Fed cuts. BTC inflows hit 25K, a 1-year low, with avg. deposit size halved since July. USDT deposits climb while altcoin inflows signal rotation. pic.twitter.com/dhDLFXeYwV — CryptoQuant.com (@cryptoquant_com) September 16, 2025 On-chain data from the firm this week paints a mixed picture of investor sentiment, with liquidity signals diverging across major assets. While Bitcoin and Ethereum exchange inflows are sliding to multi-month lows, stablecoin deposits are climbing, suggesting traders are preparing dry powder for the possibility of a policy pivot. Meanwhile, altcoin inflows are rising, hinting at either profit-taking or rotation into higher-risk tokens, reports CryptoQuant. Bitcoin Inflows Decline Bitcoin exchange inflows have dropped to their lowest levels in more than a year. The 7-day moving average now stands at 25,000 BTC, down from 51,000 BTC recorded in July. At the same time, the average deposit size per transaction has halved, falling from 1.14 BTC in mid-July to just 0.57 BTC in September. CryptoQuant analysts say this indicates reduced selling pressure from larger holders, with long-term investors showing little desire to exit positions ahead of the Fed’s decision. Ethereum Tracks Similar Trend Ethereum is mirroring Bitcoin’s subdued exchange activity. ETH inflows have fallen to a two-month low, with the 7-day average declining to 783,000 ETH, compared with 1.8 million ETH as recently as mid-August. Deposit sizes are also shrinking, with the average transaction dropping from 40–45 ETH at earlier peaks to around 30 ETH today. Taken together, the trend reflects muted sell-side activity, echoing Bitcoin’s low inflows and reinforcing the view that investors are reluctant to liquidate major holdings before a possible macro shift. Stablecoin Deposits Surge In contrast, stablecoins are showing a surge of inflows, particularly Tether (USDT). Net deposits reached $379 million on August 31, the highest level year-to-date, before easing to around $200 million more recently. Even so, the daily average USDT deposit has more than doubled, from $63,000 in July to $130,000 today. This sharp uptick implies investors are actively moving liquidity onto exchanges, preparing to deploy capital quickly if a favorable Fed outcome sparks a rally. Altcoin Activity Picks Up Altcoins are bucking the broader slowdown in inflows. Transaction deposits across a basket of non-BTC and ETH tokens have risen to 55,000 (7-day total), compared with the flat 20,000–30,000 range seen in May and June. CryptoQuant analysts note this increase could reflect heightened selling pressure as investors rotate out of riskier assets, or conversely, growing speculative interest in higher-beta tokens ahead of a potential macro catalyst. Outlook The Fed’s upcoming announcement is poised to test these liquidity patterns. Reduced BTC and ETH inflows suggest conviction among long-term holders, while higher stablecoin deposits highlight a market eager to react quickly. Whether the shift favors blue-chip crypto assets or speculative altcoins will depend heavily on the Fed’s next move. The post Investors Brace for Fed Pivot as BTC & ETH Outflows Contrast Stablecoin Surge: CryptoQuant appeared first on Cryptonews .', 'KEYWORDS': 'Blockchain News|News|CryptoQuant|Federal Reserve|Stablecoin', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEUTRAL', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758044636, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758044869, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 52, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'cryptonews', 'NAME': 'cryptonews', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/cryptonews.png', 'URL': 'https://cryptonews.com/news/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758044637, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1680604053}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 24, 'NAME': 'ETH', 'CATEGORY': 'ETH'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 210, 'NAME': 'MACROECONOMICS', 'CATEGORY': 'MACROECONOMICS'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 51825754, 'GUID': 'https://www.investing.com/news/cryptocurrency-news/fightid-and-ufc-expand-web3-collaboration-to-grow-global-fan-engagement-4240748', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758044417, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/106/default.png', 'TITLE': 'Fight.ID and UFC Expand Web3 Collaboration to Grow Global Fan Engagement', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': '', 'URL': 'https://www.investing.com/news/cryptocurrency-news/fightid-and-ufc-expand-web3-collaboration-to-grow-global-fan-engagement-4240748', 'SOURCE_ID': 106, 'BODY': '', 'KEYWORDS': '', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758033371, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758044417, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 106, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'investing_comcryptonews', 'NAME': 'Investing.com Crypto News', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/106/default.png', 'URL': 'https://www.investing.com/rss/news_301.rss', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': 1505088000, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758044748, 'CREATED_ON': 1754907212, 'UPDATED_ON': 1754907484}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 63, 'NAME': 'OTHER', 'CATEGORY': 'OTHER'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 51832704, 'GUID': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/?p=205165', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758044411, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/82/51832704.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Binance DOJ Monitoring: A Pivotal Step Towards Regulatory Relief', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Editorial Team', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinworld.co.in/binance-doj-monitoring-ends/', 'SOURCE_ID': 82, 'BODY': 'BitcoinWorld Binance DOJ Monitoring: A Pivotal Step Towards Regulatory Relief Exciting news is rippling through the cryptocurrency world, signaling a significant shift for one of its largest players. Binance, the global crypto exchange giant, is reportedly nearing a crucial agreement that would conclude its compliance oversight by the U.S. Department of Justice. This development, as reported by Bloomberg, marks a pivotal moment for the company and the broader digital asset ecosystem. The potential end of Binance DOJ monitoring could usher in a new era of stability and trust, impacting everything from operational strategies to market sentiment. Understanding the Scope of Binance DOJ Monitoring To fully appreciate this news, it is important to understand the context of the Binance DOJ monitoring . In November 2023, Binance pleaded guilty to anti-money laundering and sanctions violations. As part of a comprehensive settlement, the exchange agreed to pay a substantial fine and, crucially, submit to independent compliance monitoring by the U.S. Department of Justice. This oversight was designed to ensure Binance implemented robust anti-money laundering (AML) and know-your-customer (KYC) programs. The goal was to prevent illicit financial activities on its platform. An independent monitor was appointed to assess Binance’s adherence to these new standards and report back to the DOJ. This period of intense scrutiny has been a critical phase for Binance, forcing significant internal reforms and a stronger commitment to regulatory compliance. Why is Ending Binance DOJ Monitoring So Crucial? The reported nearing conclusion of Binance DOJ monitoring carries immense weight for several reasons. Firstly, it signifies that Binance has likely met the stringent requirements set forth by the U.S. Department of Justice. This achievement demonstrates a strengthened compliance framework and a commitment to operating within legal boundaries. Moreover, the cessation of this oversight offers tangible benefits: Operational Freedom: Binance can allocate resources previously dedicated to monitor-related tasks towards innovation and growth. Enhanced Reputation: Successfully navigating this period can significantly bolster Binance’s standing among regulators, institutions, and individual users globally. Market Confidence: Reduced regulatory uncertainty often translates into increased investor confidence, potentially attracting more institutional capital to the platform and the wider crypto market. This milestone reflects a proactive effort by Binance to mature as a financial entity, embracing necessary regulatory frameworks. What’s Next for Binance After DOJ Monitoring? With the potential end of Binance DOJ monitoring on the horizon, many are wondering what the future holds for the exchange. While the immediate pressure of external oversight may lift, Binance’s commitment to compliance will undoubtedly remain a top priority. The lessons learned and systems implemented during this period are expected to form the bedrock of its ongoing operations. Binance is likely to focus on: Sustained Compliance Efforts: Maintaining and continuously improving its internal AML and KYC protocols. Global Expansion: Pursuing licenses and expanding services in new, regulated markets. Innovation: Re-focusing on developing new products and services for its vast user base. For users and the broader crypto community, this development suggests a more stable and mature Binance. It signals a company that is serious about its responsibilities and dedicated to fostering a safer environment for digital asset trading. The news that Binance is nearing the end of its U.S. Department of Justice compliance monitoring is a testament to the company’s significant efforts in overhauling its regulatory framework. This pivotal moment not only marks a new chapter for Binance, potentially freeing it from intense scrutiny, but also sends a powerful message to the entire cryptocurrency industry. It underscores the increasing importance of robust compliance and responsible operations in the evolving digital finance landscape. As Binance steps into this new phase, the industry will be watching closely, hoping this signifies a path towards greater legitimacy and broader adoption for digital assets worldwide. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) 1. What was the original purpose of the Binance DOJ monitoring? The monitoring was imposed as part of a settlement after Binance pleaded guilty to anti-money laundering and sanctions violations in November 2023. Its purpose was to ensure Binance implemented and maintained robust compliance programs to prevent illicit financial activities. 2. How long has Binance been under DOJ monitoring? Binance has been under independent compliance monitoring by the U.S. Department of Justice since its settlement in November 2023, meaning the oversight period has lasted for several months. 3. What are the immediate implications of ending this oversight? Ending the oversight suggests Binance has met the DOJ’s compliance requirements. This could lead to increased operational freedom, an enhanced global reputation, and potentially boost market confidence in the exchange and the wider crypto industry. 4. Does this mean Binance is free from all US regulatory issues? While the specific DOJ compliance monitoring might conclude, Binance, like all major financial entities, will always be subject to ongoing regulatory scrutiny from various bodies in the US and globally. This particular agreement focuses on past violations and future compliance commitments. 5. What should Binance users know about this development? Users should view this as a positive sign of Binance’s commitment to regulatory compliance and security. It indicates a more stable and potentially safer platform for trading digital assets, as the exchange has demonstrably strengthened its internal controls. If you found this article informative, please consider sharing it with your network! Spreading awareness about key developments like the conclusion of Binance DOJ monitoring helps everyone stay informed about the evolving world of cryptocurrency regulation and its impact on major players. Your shares help us reach more readers interested in the future of digital finance. To learn more about the latest crypto market trends, explore our article on key developments shaping Binance’s institutional adoption. This post Binance DOJ Monitoring: A Pivotal Step Towards Regulatory Relief first appeared on BitcoinWorld .', 'KEYWORDS': 'Crypto News|BINANCE|Compliance|CRYPTOCURRENCY|DOJ|REGULATION', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758044430, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758044431, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 82, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'bitcoinworld', 'NAME': 'Bitcoin World', 