n’t riding on hype alone. It’s a true Layer 2, built for speed, scale, and efficiency. Transactions are near-instant, gas fees are negligible, and the system delivers exactly what Layer 1 chains can’t. But what sets it apart is how it merges that power with meme-fueled energy, creating a project that’s equal parts utility and culture. The presale comes loaded with firepower: a one million dollar giveaway and a staking system that rewards the boldest. Early buyers can grab a jaw-dropping seven hundred percent APY, but those numbers fall as more players join. It’s crypto’s version of move fast or get left behind. With the Layer 2 market projected to smash ten trillion dollars annually by 2027, Layer Brett has all the ingredients to turn early conviction into life-changing gains. The question is simple: are you willing to let Layer Brett’s opportunity pass you by? XRP Price Prediction: Understanding Market Alternatives XRP is cementing its position as a global leader in cross-border payments. With its legal clarity now secured, Ripple is signing major new partnerships with global banks and financial institutions. XRP price predictions rely on the growing demand for an XRP ETF, positioning the token to push beyond $5. Solana News Today: A Look at SOL’s Trajectory Solana is no longer just a high-speed blockchain; it’s the home of the Decentralized Physical Infrastructure Networks (DePIN) movement. This sector, which combines real-world hardware with blockchain incentives, is creating tangible utility and massive institutional interest. Solana news is full of a bullish trajectory, and even the charts show a confirmed SOL breakout. With analysts forecasting a SOL move towards the $400 range, SOL appears ready to challenge for a top-three market cap position. Layer Brett: A Better Opportunity? Layer Brett’s presale offers an early entry point at $0.0058 per $LBRETT . Early buyers can leverage substantial staking rewards and join the $1 million giveaway. With experts estimating $LBRETT to grow as much as 100x, it is presenting itself as the best crypto to buy today. Layer Brett vs. Established Cryptos While XRP price prediction and Solana news show growth for both, Layer Brett presents a unique blend of meme culture and Layer 2 utility. Its presale allows access to early staking rewards and a distinct opportunity. Head to the Layer Brett website and join the fun and utility, rolled into one! Discover More About Layer Brett ($LBRETT): Presale: LayerBrett | Fast & Rewarding Layer 2 Blockchain Telegram: View @layerbrett X: Layer Brett (@LayerBrett) / X', 'KEYWORDS': 'Press Release', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758044900, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758044901, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 43, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'cryptopolitan', 'NAME': 'Cryptopolitan', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/cryptopolitan.png', 'URL': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758044748, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1681205909}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 46, 'NAME': 'SOL', 'CATEGORY': 'SOL'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 58, 'NAME': 'XRP', 'CATEGORY': 'XRP'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 51832580, 'GUID': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/?p=810423', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758043914, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/43/51832580.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Gemini stock erases most IPO enthusiasm after sharp decline', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Florence Muchai', 'URL': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/gemini-shares-tank-6-extends-post-ipo-slump/', 'SOURCE_ID': 43, 'BODY': 'Gemini’s stock has slid 6% further, extending its losses to 24% since going public. The crypto exchange launched by Cameron and Tyler Winklevoss has seen its early IPO excitement fade as investors become cautious about its financial performance. The sharp decline follows an initial surge after the company raised $425 million in its IPO, valuing the firm at $3.3 billion before trading began. On its first day, GEMI spiked to $45.89 before closing at $32, 14% more than its offer price. However, since that high point, shares have dropped more than 34%, erasing most of the early enthusiasm from public market investors. Currently, the stock is trading at $30.42. Analysts say that Gemini is overvalued The slide comes as investors look more closely at Gemini’s financial health. The company reported a $283 million net loss in the first half of 2025, compared with a $159 million loss for all of 2024. Revenue growth has also slowed, making it harder for the stock’s high valuation to hold up. Compass Point analyst Ed Engel noted that GEMI is trading at 26 times its annualized first-half revenue. This price-to-sales (P/S) multiple is often used to gauge whether a stock is expensive, meaning investors are paying 26 dollars for every dollar the company is expected to generate in sales this year. This makes its shares look expensive compared to other companies in the same industry and the capital markets sector as a whole. In the capital markets, it shows how investors feel about the future’s growth potential, profitability, and security. This measure is especially important for businesses like Gemini Space Station that are still unprofitable and lack useful earnings data. The P/S ratio is much higher than the average for the peer group (3.2) and the industry average (4). This shows that the market may be pricing in high growth expectations or not considering financial risks. It might be hard to explain such a high price in the short term without clear proof of steady revenue growth or higher profits. Hence, the fair value is $32.52, which means it is overvalued. The broader crypto equity market is steady The broader crypto equity market has remained more stable. Robinhood reported revenues of $989 million, up 45% year on year. This print exceeded analysts’ expectations by 7.4%. Overall, it was a strong quarter for the company with an impressive beat of analysts’ EBITDA estimates and solid user growth. “We delivered strong business results in Q2 driven by relentless product velocity, and we launched tokenization—which I believe is the biggest innovation our industry has seen in the past decade,” said Vlad Tenev, Chairman and CEO of Robinhood. The stock went up 7.9% after reporting and currently trades at $114.61. However, it has been down 3% in the last week, currently trading at $116.39. Coinbase reported revenues of $1.50 billion, up 3.3% year on year. It fell short of analysts’ expectations by 4.3%. It was a disappointing quarter as it posted a significant miss of analysts’ monthly transacting users and EBITDA estimates. Coinbase delivered the weakest performance against analyst estimates in the group. The company reported 8.7 million monthly active users, up 6.1% year on year. The stock went down 13.3% after the results and currently trades at $327.39. However, it has remained flat over the week Also, the one-month return of Circle Internet Group is 11.48%, and its shares lost 17.04% of their value over the last three months. However, it is up 13% in the last week. Currently, it is trading at $135.75 per share. Join Bybit now and claim a $50 bonus in minutes', 'KEYWORDS': 'News|CRCL|Gemini', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEGATIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758044219, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758044900, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 43, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'cryptopolitan', 'NAME': 'Cryptopolitan', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/cryptopolitan.png', 'URL': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758044748, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1681205909}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 25, 'NAME': 'EXCHANGE', 'CATEGORY': 'EXCHANGE'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 51832378, 'GUID': 'https://www.investing.com/news/cryptocurrency-news/binance-in-talks-with-doj-to-drop-oversight-requirement-in-settlement-4240960', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758043878, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/106/default.png', 'TITLE': 'Binance in talks with DOJ to drop oversight requirement in settlement', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': '', 'URL': 'https://www.investing.com/news/cryptocurrency-news/binance-in-talks-with-doj-to-drop-oversight-requirement-in-settlement-4240960', 'SOURCE_ID': 106, 'BODY': '', 'KEYWORDS': '', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEUTRAL', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758043879, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 106, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'investing_comcryptonews', 'NAME': 'Investing.com Crypto News', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/106/default.png', 'URL': 'https://www.investing.com/rss/news_301.rss', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': 1505088000, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758044748, 'CREATED_ON': 1754907212, 'UPDATED_ON': 1754907484}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 74, 'NAME': 'BNB', 'CATEGORY': 'BNB'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 25, 'NAME': 'EXCH